DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T235959
UID:festival-international-virtual-augmented-reality-stories@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:FIVARS returns to Toronto from June 15 to 19\, 2026\, for its 
 12th edition\, with OCAD U as presenting sponsor.\n\nFIVARS (Festival of I
 nternational Virtual and Augmented Reality Stories) returns to Toronto fro
 m June 15 to 19\, 2026\, for its 12th edition\, with OCAD University as pr
 esenting sponsor and first-time venue host at 49 McCaul St. As Canada’s 
 original festival dedicated to immersive storytelling\, FIVARS showcases b
 oundary-pushing formats—from spatialized audio and live VR performance t
 o projection mapping and WebXR experiences. More info at https://fivars.ne
 t/
LOCATION:49 McCaul St. (MCG) 49 McCaul St.
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/festival-international-vir
 tual-augmented-reality-stories
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:OCAD U Gala
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T235900
UID:ocad-u-gala@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Convening Toronto's most creative and influential minds in the
  art and design sector\, the OCAD U Gala returns this spring!\n\nGET READY
  TO EXPERIENCE TORONTO’S FAST-GROWING ART AND DESIGN EVENT Celebrating t
 he talent and creativity of artists and designers in support of students a
 t OCAD University.\n\nFollowing a standout debut last spring\, the OCAD U 
 Gala returns on May 27\, 2026 \, as a rising highlight in Toronto’s cult
 ural calendar. This annual event brings together the city’s most creativ
 e thinkers for an immersive evening that showcases visionary ideas\, excep
 tional talent and the vibrant spirit of our University. With the support o
 f our generous sponsors\, guests will experience striking art activations\
 , bold design moments and an atmosphere alive with energy—reflecting the
  gala’s growing momentum as one of Toronto’s premier art and design ce
 lebrations.\n\nThe Event at a Glance VIP Reception Art Installations and E
 xperiences Dinner and Program Live Art Auction After Party For one night o
 nly\, guests will have the opportunity to bid on one-of-a-kind artwork by 
 an inspiring mix of emerging talent and established artists. All OCAD U al
 umni. Featuring: Pardiss Amerian\, Wendy Coburn\, Mitchell Fenton\, Camill
 e Jodoin-Eng\, Alexa Kumiko Hatanaka\, Megan McCabe\, Jordin Mimran\, Kris
 tine Moran\, Kristín Morthens\, Kyle Scheurmann\, John Scott\, Rosalie Sh
 arp\, Pixie Shaw\, Bewabon Shilling\, and Kendra Yee. Don’t miss your ch
 ance to be part of this exclusive event in the heart of Toronto’s vibran
 t art and design scene.\n\n2026 Art Auction Catalogue\n\nInside the Collec
 tion\n\nAdvancing Student Success Funds raised at the gala will establish 
 vital student bursaries at OCAD U that reduce financial barriers to a lead
 ing art and design university education. This crucial support fosters the 
 growth and talent of future creative leaders and innovators.\n\nBuy Gala T
 ickets\n\nThe celebration continues at the OCAD U Gala After Party! Experi
 ence the energy of the OCAD U community alongside Toronto’s most creativ
 e and influential minds in a vibrant\, immersive atmosphere filled with mu
 sic\, art\, cocktails and gourmet desserts. Tickets are available for purc
 hase now. Spots are limited—get yours before they’re gone! Dress Code:
  Creative Cocktail *Note: If you’ve already purchased a ticket or are at
 tending the OCAD U Gala\, your entry to the After Party is free.\n\nBuy Af
 ter Party Tickets\n\nThe OCAD U Gala Committee\n\nWe are grateful to our d
 edicated Gala Committee members\, whose vision and leadership are helping 
 bring this extraordinary event to life.\n\nAmy Burstyn-Fritz\, Co-Founder 
 of Misette - Co-Chair\n\nJeff Hull\, President\, Hullmark - Co-Chair\n\nCo
 lleen Baldwin Chris Braden Jaclyn Cobourn Alison Currie Rana Florida Alan 
 Gertner Nandini Gupta Alison Milne Jordin Mimran Tanya Taylor\n\nHighlight
 s from the Inaugural OCAD U Gala\n\nTHANK YOU TO OUR OCAD U GALA SPONSORS
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street
URL:https://can01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fsecu
 re3.convio.net%2Focadu%2Fsite%2FTicketing%3Fview%3DTickets%26id%3D102173&d
 ata=05%7C02%7Cwebsupport%40ocadu.ca%7C465295de16a74bff2eff08de845602e2%7C0
 6e469d12d2a468fae9b7df0968eb6d7%7C0%7C0%7C639093702745936498%7CUnknown%7CT
 WFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkF
 OIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=lWAztG2H92Ve3uK4oLKZcN%2B
 VyIfZfwlZSqCVPycCY%2Fw%3D&reserved=0
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:OCAD University Senate Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T151500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T181500
UID:ocad-university-senate-meeting-17@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:OCAD University Senate Meeting\n\nThe next regular meeting of 
 the OCAD University Senate is scheduled to take place on Monday\, May 25\,
  2026 from 3:15 pm – 6:15 pm EDT. The Senate is responsible for the esta
 blishment and regulation of academic policy\, standards and procedures at 
 OCAD University. The Senate and its many committees are in charge of all m
 atters pertaining to OCAD U academic resources\, academic programming\, ac
 ademic strategic planning\, student affairs and any other such matters rel
 ating to academic issues. More information can be found on the OCAD U Sena
 te webpage . If you would like to attend as a guest\, or if you have any q
 uestions\, please contact David Wagschal\, Quality Assurance Officer & Ass
 ociate Senate Secretary at dwagschal@ocadu.ca.
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/ocad-university-senate-mee
 ting-17
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Forest Therapy Session with Sock Gee
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T150000
UID:forest-therapy-session-sock-gee@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Forest Therapy Session with Sock Gee\n\nWander slowly\, breath
 e deeply\, and gather in ritual. This small-group meditative nature walk a
 nd tea ceremony invites participants into a quiet\, sensory experience roo
 ted in mindfulness\, presence\, and environmental connection—an intimate
  offering for up to 10 guests. To register\, please email Susan Jama at su
 sanjama@ocadu.ca About Sock Gee Sock Gee is a Certified Forest Therapy Gui
 de through the Association on Nature and Forest Therapy Guides and Program
 s. A resident of Mississauga who loves to wander and explore in nature\, s
 he is eager to share the many benefits of Forest Bathing with the communit
 y. Sock Gee believes that re-membering that we are part of nature leads to
  harmonious relationship with others and the more-than human world. Becomi
 ng (in the light of the miracle) is generously supported by the Ontario Ar
 ts Council\, an agency of the Government of Ontario through the Curatorial
  Projects: Indigenous and Culturally Diverse program. Onsite Gallery is ge
 nerously supported by The Delaney Family.
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/forest-therapy-session-soc
 k-gee
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Getting NowHere
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T170000
UID:getting-nowhere@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:In this exhibition\, Prof. Emerit Stan Krzyzanowski will exhib
 it work that has been pivotal in his art practice. Some have never been sh
 own before. The exhibition/residency comes from a recent decision to becom
 e a founding member of LUCID\, a new artist-run co-op and exhibition space
  in Hamilton\, Ontario.\n\nIn this exhibition\, Prof. Emerit Stan Krzyzano
 wski will exhibit work that has been pivotal in his art practice. Some hav
 e never been shown before. The exhibition/residency comes from a recent de
 cision to become a founding member of LUCID\, a new artist-run co-op and e
 xhibition space in Hamilton\, Ontario. Artwork ( Cone Oscillator ): As the
  pine cone on the Cone Oscillator dries it slowly opens and a toothpick ex
 tension fastened to one of its scales presses a switch\, activating a moto
 r. A water bottle above is squeezed and the pine cone receives a shower. N
 ow wet\, the pine cone closes quickly. Over time\, it slowly dries\, opens
  and reactivates the motor\, triggering another shower so that the entire 
 process repeats. See the Cone Oscillator in action . Exhibition opening : 
 Saturday\, May 9\, 12 to 5 p.m. Exhibition schedule : May 7 to 10\, 12 to 
 5 p.m. and May 14 to 17\, 12 to 5 p.m. Artist Talk : Saturday\, May 9\, 2 
 p.m.
LOCATION:Off Campus LUCID Artspace\, 837 King St. E\,\, Hamilton. Enter at
  the rear of the building. Once you arrive at the back door of the buildin
 g\, please text the number posted on the door for entry.
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/getting-nowhere
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GradEx 111
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260506T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260510T235959
UID:gradex-111@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:OCAD University’s 111th Annual Graduate Exhibition\, Toronto
 ’s largest free art and design exhibition\, takes place May 6 to 10\, 20
 26\, featuring the work of more than 800 emerging artists and designers.\n
 \nDon’t miss GradEx 111\, OCAD University’s 111th Annual Graduate Exhi
 bition – Toronto’s largest free art and design exhibition from May 6 t
 o 10\, 2026. Be inspired by the work of more than 800 emerging artists and
  designers at OCAD U’s 100 McCaul St. location. A supplemental online ex
 hibition will also launch on May 6. Learn more about GradEx 111
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street
URL:https://ocadu.ca/gradex
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GradEx 2026 Plinth Sign-out
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260421T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T235959
UID:gradex-2026-plinth-sign-out@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Plinth Protocol for GradEx 2026\n\nMCA 225A is located at the 
 back of the Ada Slaight Gallery (highlighted in pink on map). Plinths can 
 only be booked in person and during limited times . Visit MCA 225A during 
 the following reservation periods (dates/times may be subject to change so
  check this page 2 days prior to arriving): Tuesday April 21 : 1:00 - 1:30
  pm Tuesday April 28 : 1:00 - 1:30 pm Monday May 4 : 1:00 - 1:30 pm A maxi
 mum of 2 plinths per student can be booked during each reservation period.
  If you require more than 2 plinths\, return the following week and upon a
 vailability you may book 2 more at a time. Plinths can be picked up during
  any of the reservation times listed above\, but you must pick it up by Ma
 y 4\, 1:30pm or your reservation is considered abandoned and it may be giv
 en to someone else. All plinths must be returned to the Ada Slaight Galler
 y no later than May 13 . You may leave them there at any time after GradEx
  with your information taped to the plinth(s). No email requests will be g
 ranted\, must be booked in person. OCAD U ID card is required. If student 
 cannot book in person another student or Faculty may reserve plinths on th
 eir behalf\, but it will be under their name. You must provide the room nu
 mber you will be exhibiting in. Plinths must be returned in the condition 
 you received them in or better. A fee of $150 will be charged for each unr
 eturned or severely damaged plinth.
LOCATION:Ada Slaight Student Gallery 100 McCaul St. 2nd floor
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/gradex-2026-plinth-sign-ou
 t
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
